{
  "name": "damselfly",
  "_about": "A damselfly -- the azure damselfly (Coenagrion puella), a male 3.3 cm long: slender as a needle; a wide hammer of a head with the eyes far apart at its ends, blue, with pale spots behind them; a small slanted thorax, sky blue with black stripes; a very long thin abdomen, blue ringed black, a black U on its second segment, the tip black and blue; four narrow stalked wings, clear with a small dark pterostigma near each tip, held closed together over the abdomen at rest; thin bristly black legs set forward. Coats: the female (green and black), the banded demoiselle (metallic blue-green, a dark band across the wings). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/others.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, antennae that wave; the wings at rest as the animal holds them, beating in the variant \"flying\").",
